            "review_text": "nguyen2612\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam1 contribution\n0\nGood Taste but Bad Air Conditional\nDec 2017 • Friends\nThaiExpress is one of the restaurants have traditional food of Thailand in Vincom center. I went here at the Christmas day in the evening and go with my girlfriend and her cousin.This essay will explore the review this restaurant - the taste of food, the timing for the service and atmosphere -- before I recommend for this restaurant or not.\n\nThe taste of food is very delicious. I was called rice with pork and Thai-basil. The smell of Thai-basil is pretty good but it also spicy. Most of the dish in here is always spicy. I went with my friends and have one guy, he can’t eat spicy food. When I ask the service that can they make the food just have a little bit spicy, they said “No, they can’t because that is the main savory of the food in here “ so that is boring. But overall the food in here is very delicious and good of smell.\n\nThe timing for the service to serve the food is long . I went here on Christmas day and have so many people come here to eat too. With that reason, I can understand that why they serve the food too long. The final dish takes 30 minutes to get on our table.\n\nThe atmosphere in here is so hot.This restaurant with mostly spicy food but we can’t eat with the hot atmosphere, that so terrible. I think this is the big problem with this restaurant, the air conditioner is too weak and makes the customer feel not good when they eat.\n\nOverall, with me, this restaurant is 7 on 10 points because of the delicious food but poor service and atmosphere. I’ll recommend this restaurant but never recommend for anybody can’t eat spicy food.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten December 26, 2017",
